IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uro-nouns`

-- Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2026 (S.I. 2026/148): THE TITLE BLOCK AND PART 1 (INTRODUCTION).
-- Layer 1. Dates are data (the brief): the date the Order was made, every date article 1(3) fixes, the
-- rules that make some of them depend on the beneficiary, and the extent of each provision (art 1(2)).
-- Article 1(1) (the citation) is not encoded: it is a pure citation (NOTES.md, coverage table).
-- Article 7 (the dates on which the changes take effect) is in uro-part2-effect-dates.
--
-- "benefit week" and "assessment period" are defined OUTSIDE the text (art 1(3)(g) to (n) say so, citing
-- the Income Support, JSA, State Pension Credit and ESA Regulations and the Welfare Reform Act 2012). A
-- person's first benefit week is therefore a plain input DATE: "out of text".

§ `Title block`

-- src:1 | 2026 No. 148
-- src:2 | SOCIAL SECURITY TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT
-- src:3 | The Social Security Benefits Up-rating Order 2026
-- src:4 | Made 2nd March 2026
-- src:5 | Coming into force in accordance with article 1(3) and (4)
@ref title block (src:1-5)
`title block: the date on which the Order was made` MEANS YMD 2026 3 2

§ `Article 1 -- Citation, extent, commencement and effect`

§§ `Article 1(2) -- extent`

-- src:14 | (2) This Order extends to England and Wales and Scotland, save for the following provisions which extend to England and Wales only—
-- src:15 | (a) paragraphs (3) and (5) in so far as they provide for the coming into force, or taking effect, dates for the provisions mentioned in sub-paragraphs (b) to (e) of this paragraph;
-- src:16 | (b) article 3, in so far as it either states or increases the sums specified in—
-- src:17 | (i) Part III of Schedule 4 to the Contributions and Benefits Act for attendance allowance, severe disablement allowance, age related addition and carer’s allowance;
-- src:18 | (ii) Part IV of Schedule 4 to that Act for the increase for an adult dependant payable with severe disablement allowance; and
-- src:19 | (iii) Part V of Schedule 4 to that Act;
-- src:20 | (c) article 7, in so far as it specifies the taking into effect dates for the provision made in article 3 as to the sums specified in the provisions referred to in sub-paragraph (b) of this paragraph;
-- src:21 | (d) article 14; and
-- src:22 | (e) article 15.
@ref art 1(2) (src:14-22)
DECLARE `a territory` IS ONE OF
    `England and Wales`
    `Scotland`

-- One constructor for the provisions of the Order that extend everywhere, and one for each provision that
-- art 1(2)(a) to (e) says extends to England and Wales only.
@ref art 1(2)(a) to (e) (src:14-22)
DECLARE `a provision whose extent art 1(2) states` IS ONE OF
    `any provision not listed in art 1(2)(a) to (e)`
    `art 1(3) and (5), as to the dates for the provisions in art 1(2)(b) to (e)`
    `art 3, as to the Part III sums for attendance allowance, severe disablement allowance, age related addition and carer's allowance`
    `art 3, as to the Part IV increase for an adult dependant payable with severe disablement allowance`
    `art 3, as to the Part V sums`
    `art 7, as to the dates for the sums in art 1(2)(b)`
    `art 14`
    `art 15`

@ref art 1(2) (src:14-22)
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `a provision whose extent art 1(2) states`
      `the territory` IS A `a territory`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art 1(2): the provision extends to the territory` `the provision` `the territory` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `any provision not listed in art 1(2)(a) to (e)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `the territory` EQUALS `England and Wales`

