§§ `Article 1(4) -- universal credit and unearned income`

-- out of text: Welfare Reform Act 2012 s 7(2) ('assessment period'): whether a universal credit award is in force and whether the question is about unearned income under it are inputs.
-- (4) overrides the dates in (3) for these thirteen articles, but only "for the purposes of determining the
-- beneficiary's unearned income in relation to" a universal credit award in force for the beneficiary: the
-- date is then the (3)(n) date. Anything else: NOTHING (this paragraph does not apply; (3) does).
-- src:41 | (4) In so far as articles 3, 4, 5, 6, 9, 11, 12, 13, 16, 17, 18, 28 and 31 relate to a beneficiary in favour of whom an award of universal credit is in force, those articles shall come into force for the purposes of determining the beneficiary’s unearned income in relation to that award on the same day as articles 32 and 33 come into force for that beneficiary.
@ref art 1(4) (src:41)
GIVEN `the article` IS A NUMBER
      `a universal credit award is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is unearned income under that award` IS A BOOLEAN
      `first day of first assessment period on or after 6th April 2026` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`art 1(4): the date on which the article comes into force for the beneficiary's unearned income under a universal credit award` `the article` `a universal credit award is in force` `the purpose is unearned income under that award` `first day of first assessment period on or after 6th April 2026` MEANS
    IF     elem `the article` (LIST 3, 4, 5, 6, 9, 11, 12, 13, 16, 17, 18, 28, 31)
       AND `a universal credit award is in force`
       AND `the purpose is unearned income under that award`
    THEN `art 1(3)(n): the date on which articles 32 and 33 come into force for the beneficiary` `first day of first assessment period on or after 6th April 2026`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Article 1(3) and (4) together -- the date for a given article`

-- out of text: the 'benefit week' and 'assessment period' instruments listed above for art 1(3)(g) to (n); Housing Benefit Regulations 'rent'; Contributions and Benefits Act s 35A(1): each is an input of this rule.
-- "(3) Subject to paragraphs (4) and (5)": (4) is tried first. The article number is a plain input; the facts
-- that matter are the beneficiary's own. NOTHING means the text gives no date for that article number or
-- the benefit-week or assessment-period date given is not on or after 6th April 2026.
@ref art 1(3) and (4) (src:23-41)
GIVEN `the article` IS A NUMBER
      `the increase is an article 7(9)(b) increase` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is the maternity allowance rate under section 35A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `rent is payable weekly or at a multiple of a week` IS A BOOLEAN
      `first day of first benefit week on or after 6th April 2026` IS A DATE
      `a universal credit award is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is unearned income under that award` IS A BOOLEAN
      `first day of first assessment period on or after 6th April 2026` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`art 1(3) and (4): the date on which the article comes into force for the beneficiary` `the article` `the increase is an article 7(9)(b) increase` `the purpose is the maternity allowance rate under section 35A(1)` `rent is payable weekly or at a multiple of a week` `first day of first benefit week on or after 6th April 2026` `a universal credit award is in force` `the purpose is unearned income under that award` `first day of first assessment period on or after 6th April 2026` MEANS
    CONSIDER `art 1(4): the date on which the article comes into force for the beneficiary's unearned income under a universal credit award` `the article` `a universal credit award is in force` `the purpose is unearned income under that award` `first day of first assessment period on or after 6th April 2026`
        WHEN JUST d THEN JUST d
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            BRANCH
                IF elem `the article` (LIST 1, 2, 7)
                THEN JUST (`art 1(3)(a): the date on which articles 1, 2 and 7 come into force`)
                IF `the article` EQUALS 3
                THEN JUST (`art 1(3)(b): the date on which article 3 comes into force` `the increase is an article 7(9)(b) increase`)
                IF elem `the article` (LIST 4, 6, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 18, 19)
                THEN JUST (`art 1(3)(c): the date on which articles 4, 6, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 18 and 19 come into force`)
                IF elem `the article` (LIST 5, 8)
                THEN JUST (`art 1(3)(d): the date on which articles 5 and 8 come into force`)
                IF `the article` EQUALS 9
                THEN JUST (`art 1(3)(e): the date on which article 9 comes into force` `the purpose is the maternity allowance rate under section 35A(1)`)
                IF elem `the article` (LIST 16, 17)
                THEN JUST (`art 1(3)(f): the date on which articles 16 and 17 come into force`)
                IF elem `the article` (LIST 20, 21, 22)
                THEN `art 1(3)(g): the date on which articles 20, 21 and 22 come into force for the beneficiary` `first day of first benefit week on or after 6th April 2026`
                IF elem `the article` (LIST 23, 24)
                THEN JUST (`art 1(3)(h): the date on which articles 23 and 24 come into force` `rent is payable weekly or at a multiple of a week`)
                IF elem `the article` (LIST 25, 26, 27)
                THEN `art 1(3)(i): the date on which articles 25, 26 and 27 come into force for the beneficiary` `first day of first benefit week on or after 6th April 2026`
                IF `the article` EQUALS 28
                THEN `art 1(3)(j): the date on which article 28 comes into force for the beneficiary` `first day of first benefit week on or after 6th April 2026`
                IF `the article` EQUALS 29
                THEN `art 1(3)(k): the date on which article 29 comes into force for the beneficiary` `first day of first benefit week on or after 6th April 2026`
                IF `the article` EQUALS 30
                THEN `art 1(3)(l): the date on which article 30 comes into force for the beneficiary` `first day of first benefit week on or after 6th April 2026`
                IF `the article` EQUALS 31
                THEN `art 1(3)(m): the date on which article 31 comes into force for the beneficiary` `first day of first benefit week on or after 6th April 2026`
                IF elem `the article` (LIST 32, 33)
                THEN `art 1(3)(n): the date on which articles 32 and 33 come into force for the beneficiary` `first day of first assessment period on or after 6th April 2026`
                IF `the article` EQUALS 34
                THEN JUST (`art 1(3)(o): the date on which article 34 comes into force`)
                OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Article 1(5) -- taking effect`

-- src:42 | (5) The changes made in the sums specified for rates or amounts of benefit in—
-- src:43 | (a) articles 3, 4, 5, 6, 11, 12 and 13; and
-- src:44 | (b) article 25(b), in so far as that sum is relevant for the purposes of establishing whether the rate of any benefit is not to be increased in respect of an adult dependant because the earnings of the dependant exceed a specified amount,
-- src:45 | shall take effect for each case on the date specified in relation to that case in article 7.
@ref art 1(5) (src:42-45)
GIVEN `the article` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum is the article 25(b) adult dependant earnings sum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`art 1(5): the change in the sums takes effect on the date article 7 specifies` `the article` `the sum is the article 25(b) adult dependant earnings sum` MEANS
        elem `the article` (LIST 3, 4, 5, 6, 11, 12, 13)
    OR  (`the article` EQUALS 25 AND `the sum is the article 25(b) adult dependant earnings sum`)

§ `Article 2 -- Interpretation`

-- The Order's short names for the instruments it amends. Only the title they stand for is carried; art 2
-- decides nothing for a beneficiary, so the seat asks no question about it.
-- src:46 | 2 Interpretation
-- src:47 | In this Order—
-- src:48 | “the Computation of Earnings Regulations” means the Social Security Benefit (Computation of Earnings) Regulations 1996;
-- src:49 | “the Contributions and Benefits Act” means the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992;
-- src:50 | “the ESA Regulations 2008” means the Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008;
-- src:51 | “the ESA Regulations 2013” means the Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2013;
-- src:52 | “the ESA and UC Regulations 2017” means the Employment and Support Allowance and Universal Credit (Miscellaneous Amendments and Transitional and Savings Provisions) Regulations 2017;
-- src:53 | “the Housing Benefit Regulations” means the Housing Benefit Regulations 2006;
-- src:54 | “the Housing Benefit (SPC) Regulations” means the Housing Benefit (Persons who have attained the qualifying age for state pension credit) Regulations 2006;
-- src:55 | “the Income Support Regulations” means the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987;
-- src:56 | “the JSA Regulations 1996” means the Jobseeker’s Allowance Regulations 1996;
-- src:57 | “the JSA Regulations 2013” means the Jobseeker’s Allowance Regulations 2013;
-- src:58 | “the Pensions Act” means the Pensions Act 2014;
-- src:59 | “the Pension Schemes Act” means the Pension Schemes Act 1993;
-- src:60 | “the State Pension Credit Regulations” means the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002; and
-- src:61 | “the Universal Credit Regulations” means the Universal Credit Regulations 2013.
@ref art 2 (src:46-61)
DECLARE `a short name defined by art 2` IS ONE OF
    `the Computation of Earnings Regulations`
    `the Contributions and Benefits Act`
    `the ESA Regulations 2008`
    `the ESA Regulations 2013`
    `the ESA and UC Regulations 2017`
    `the Housing Benefit Regulations`
    `the Housing Benefit (SPC) Regulations`
    `the Income Support Regulations`
    `the JSA Regulations 1996`
    `the JSA Regulations 2013`
    `the Pensions Act`
    `the Pension Schemes Act`
    `the State Pension Credit Regulations`
    `the Universal Credit Regulations`

@ref art 2 (src:46-61)
GIVEN `which short name` IS A `a short name defined by art 2`
GIVETH A STRING
`art 2: the instrument that the short name means` `which short name` MEANS
    CONSIDER `which short name`
    WHEN `the Computation of Earnings Regulations` THEN "the Social Security Benefit (Computation of Earnings) Regulations 1996"
    WHEN `the Contributions and Benefits Act` THEN "the Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992"
    WHEN `the ESA Regulations 2008` THEN "the Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2008"
    WHEN `the ESA Regulations 2013` THEN "the Employment and Support Allowance Regulations 2013"
    WHEN `the ESA and UC Regulations 2017` THEN "the Employment and Support Allowance and Universal Credit (Miscellaneous Amendments and Transitional and Savings Provisions) Regulations 2017"
    WHEN `the Housing Benefit Regulations` THEN "the Housing Benefit Regulations 2006"
    WHEN `the Housing Benefit (SPC) Regulations` THEN "the Housing Benefit (Persons who have attained the qualifying age for state pension credit) Regulations 2006"
    WHEN `the Income Support Regulations` THEN "the Income Support (General) Regulations 1987"
    WHEN `the JSA Regulations 1996` THEN "the Jobseeker’s Allowance Regulations 1996"
    WHEN `the JSA Regulations 2013` THEN "the Jobseeker’s Allowance Regulations 2013"
    WHEN `the Pensions Act` THEN "the Pensions Act 2014"
    WHEN `the Pension Schemes Act` THEN "the Pension Schemes Act 1993"
    WHEN `the State Pension Credit Regulations` THEN "the State Pension Credit Regulations 2002"
    WHEN `the Universal Credit Regulations` THEN "the Universal Credit Regulations 2013"

